														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3675595">
									

<p>There's a lot I really like going on here - the concept and the execution of the format screw are both really working for me - but what's holding me back from an upvote is that it goes into too much detail. The direct letter from the ghosts is specifically what killed it for me - the changed text being technically just a restatement of what was already there is a really cool, original, cryptic way for the spirits to communicate; the direct threatening message was too on-the-nose, and I don't think it added nearly enough to make up for taking away the mystique the way it does. I felt similarly about the O5 note at the end. This was really evoking eerie, sentimental feelings that I think would be better served by leaving both of those out to be a little more mysterious (the other sections are already pretty clear about what's going on anyway, IMO).</p>
<p>This is still a fantastically well crafted article, and even the parts I didn't like are beautifully written - I think it would be a masterpiece without them.</p>

							</div>

								
					
